' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' The automated pass reads data members and nothing else, so a class whose
' content is methods arrives as an empty box, a facet of free functions does
' not arrive at all, and static constants inside a struct are skipped. The
' blocks below fill those boxes and draw the relationships the automated pass
' cannot see.
'
' They use fully-qualified class names rather than a reopened namespace block,
' because this PlantUML version crashes when a namespace that already holds
' classes is declared a second time. Redeclaring a class merges its members
' into the box the automated pass already drew, so a refresh keeps both.

class ores::utility::compression::gzip {
    {static} +compress(input : span<const char>) : vector<char>
    {static} +decompress(input : span<const char>) : vector<char>
}
note top of "ores::utility::compression::gzip"
Free functions: the one gzip implementation in the tree. ores.nats
and ores.storage call it instead of linking zlib themselves.
end note

